  h1: string;
}

const { h1 } = Astro.props;
---
  <h1>{h1}</h1>

<h2 id="resumen">Summary <i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> </h2>

<p>
  Web system for an online supermarket that brings together the customer experience —with purchases, history, 
  favorites, filters and PDF receipts— and an admin panel for managing 
  products, deals, user roles and sales reports, offering a complete solution from 
  purchase to internal management.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>GitHub repository <i class="fab fa-github"></i>: </strong>
  <a href="https://github.com/Franco2900/Practica-5---Supermercado" target="_blank">Practice 5</a>
</p>

<h2 id="tecnologias">Technologies used <i class="bi bi-laptop"></i> </h2>

<div class="row">

  <div class="col-4">
    Backend: <br>
    NodeJS <i class="fab fa-node-js"></i> with the Express framework 
  </div>

  <div class="col-4">
    Database: <br>
    SQL <i class="fas fa-database"></i>
  </div>
  
  <div class="col-4">
    Frontend: <br>
    Bootstrap <i class="fab fa-bootstrap"></i> and React <i class="fab fa-react"></i>
  </div>
  
</div>
<br>

<h2 id="descripcion">Full project description <i class="fas fa-align-left"></i> </h2>

<p>

Website for an online supermarket where customers can buy products and deals, view detailed versions of them and mark them as favorites. Products marked as favorites always appear first in the list of products to buy so the customer can buy them faster. The selected products and deals are added to a cart where the customer can remove anything they don't want or added by mistake and/or change the quantity to buy. 
<br /><br />
Purchases can be seen in the purchase history, which has a tool to filter purchases by date (by default the purchase history shows the newest purchases first). The history also lets the user download a PDF file as a receipt for each purchase, showing what was bought, how much was bought, the cost and the purchase date.
<br /><br />
For every action the customer takes, notifications are sent so they know their requests were confirmed/completed. 
<br /><br />
Admins, for their part, can do all these actions, plus create, delete and modify products and deals, change user roles from customer to admin or the other way around, and access reports such as earnings from the best-selling products, monthly earnings, number of sales, etc. This makes it possible to manage the supermarket completely from the same platform.
<br /><br />
In short, the project integrates both the user and the admin side, showing a complete web application that covers the whole flow of an online supermarket: from purchase to internal management.
<br /><br />

<strong>NOTE: CUSTOMER DATA IS SAMPLE DATA, NOT REAL.</strong>

</p>


